{
  "loaded": [
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::whoami",
      "description": "Your address, role, budget, direct reports, open tasks, outstanding delegations and charter.",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::services",
      "description": "The standing services you can request from your direct reports and the ones you offer, with contract and\n        playbook versions, inputs, budget per request and the record so far (requests, outcomes, runs, feedback).",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::status",
      "description": "The whole organization as a tree: each agent's role, state, budget and workload.",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::blueprint_example",
      "description": "A ready-to-edit blueprint (YAML with a comment on every field and a one-paragraph schema summary).\n\n        kind: \"research\" (facts from the web with source URLs, fact-checked), \"documents\" (write from the user's local\n        files, no web; uses `needs.inputs`, read-only folders), \"code\" (software in a repo workspace, with tests and\n        local commits) or \"analysis\" (the user's data files, read-only, analysed by a checked script). Replace every\n        <PLACEHOLDER> with what the user told you (ask for what is missing; do not invent lists), delete what does not apply, then call propose_org with the text. Read-only.\n\n        service: true for work the user wants again and again (\"every week\", \"whenever I...\"): the template then offers it\n        as a standing service (`services:` with inputs, acceptance, deliverable and budget per request, and an optional\n        first request) instead of a one-off `task:`.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "kind": {
            "default": "research",
            "title": "Kind",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "service": {
            "default": false,
            "title": "Service",
            "type": "boolean"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::propose_org",
      "description": "Validate a blueprint and return the plan the user must approve. Writes nothing; safe to call repeatedly.\n\n        blueprint: YAML or JSON text (never a file path). Start from blueprint_example(kind) for a template with every\n        field explained. Schema: `mission` (one paragraph); `needs` {scope, deliverable {description, format,\n        max_words, path (absolute)}, quality_bar, sources, inputs (read-only folders), workspace (the one absolute\n        folder agents may write in), budget_runs (the user's cap), models {cheap, strong} (optional: none = every agent on claude-sonnet-5.5), model_policy, review\n        (true/false), approval, progress, kind (research|writing|code), code {tests, packaging, commits}}; `agents`:\n        ONE top-level agent (template manager) with `children`; each agent has name and a template (manager,\n        researcher, writer, reviewer, fact-checker, engineer, tester, code-reviewer, analyst, data-checker) or a charter, and optionally\n        model, tools, workspace, scale; `task` {to, title, goal, acceptance: list of exact, checkable criteria}; optional\n        `services` (recurring work the top agent offers on request): [{name, description, inputs: [{name, description,\n        required}], acceptance, deliverable {description, format, max_words, path}, budget (runs per request), playbook,\n        locked}], in which case `task` may be omitted or be a first request {service, inputs: {name: value}, title}.\n        Works before the organization exists. Returns (1) a block headed \"PLAN FOR YOU\": show it to the user exactly\n        as written and wait for their explicit approval; (2) Details, the full plan for you; (3) a plan_id that\n        apply_org requires. If the plan has errors, fix the blueprint and propose again; never ask the user to approve\n        a plan with errors.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "blueprint": {
            "title": "Blueprint",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "blueprint"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "not_found": [],
  "note": "These tools are now loaded for the rest of this session. To RUN one, call tool_call with { \"tool_id\": \"namespace::tool\", \"arguments\": { ... } } (use the tool_id shown for each result, and arguments matching its input_schema). Do not call tool_load again for tools you have already loaded."
}

{
  "loaded": [
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::create_org",
      "description": "Create the organization this server is bound to (only possible while none exists).\n\n        mission: what the organization is for, in a few sentences. default_model: kiro model for all agents\n        (optional; unset = claude-sonnet-5.5). path: absolute directory; only needed (and only accepted) when the server is not bound to\n        one by ORG_ROOT. The directory must be missing or empty. Afterwards every tool works, no restart needed.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "mission": {
            "title": "Mission",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "default_model": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Default Model"
          },
          "path": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Path"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "mission"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::apply_org",
      "description": "Create the agents of a blueprint and give its first task. Only after the user approved the plan.\n\n        blueprint: the YAML/JSON text the user approved via propose_org (unchanged). approved: pass True only after\n        the user explicitly approved that plan in this conversation; otherwise nothing happens. plan_id: the id that\n        propose_org returned for exactly this blueprint; a missing or different id is refused (propose again, show the\n        PLAN FOR YOU block, get approval). Needs an existing organization (create_org first if there is none).\n        Refuses with the issues if the blueprint has errors or a name is taken, and undoes everything if it fails\n        midway. Returns what was created (agents, services, the first task or request); then call start() (not when\n        the blueprint gave no first task: the services wait for request(service, inputs)).\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "blueprint": {
            "title": "Blueprint",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "approved": {
            "default": false,
            "title": "Approved",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "plan_id": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Plan Id"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "blueprint"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::request",
      "description": "Ask a direct report for one of its services (see `services`): a task built from the contract.\n\n        inputs: {input name: value}; required ones must be present. note: free text for the owner. extra_acceptance:\n        criteria added after the contract's (the contract's always apply). budget: runs handed down (default: the\n        contract's; the usual reserve rule applies). revises: id of an earlier request of this service to send back for\n        rework; the reply then states the case total (runs used by the whole chain, runs handed down, the contract's\n        budget per request) and tells you to inform the user when the case exceeds that budget.\n        source (with revises): \"human\" when the user asked for this rework\n        (a rework after their own rejection, carrying their corrections, is one), \"relayed\" (the default) when it is your\n        own reading; the owner sees which.\n        Returns the task id; the result comes back like any result, then rate it with `feedback`.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "service": {
            "title": "Service",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "inputs": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "additionalProperties": true,
                "type": "object"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Inputs"
          },
          "title": {
            "default": "",
            "title": "Title",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "note": {
            "default": "",
            "title": "Note",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "extra_acceptance": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Extra Acceptance"
          },
          "budget": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Budget"
          },
          "revises": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Revises"
          },
          "source": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Source"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "service"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::start",
      "description": "Start the scheduler for this organization in the background; it wakes agents that have mail.\n\n        max_runs: stop starting agent runs after this many (safety cap; default: no cap). until_done (default True):\n        the scheduler exits by itself when you have no open task and nothing is running or can run, so you need not\n        stop it (status and progress then say \"scheduler: stopped (finished: no open tasks)\"); start it again after\n        giving the org more work. It also exits by itself, after a few minutes (`until_done_grace_seconds`), when every\n        open task is waiting for YOU (an agent is out of budget or keeps failing, or a task is stalled): status and\n        progress then say \"stopped (waiting on you: ...)\" with your options. start() refuses while that is the case:\n        grant runs first (send(to=<agent>, body=<why>, budget=N)). False keeps it running until stop(). Refused if one\n        is already running. Output goes to .runtime/scheduler.log. Returns the scheduler's pid.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "max_runs": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Max Runs"
          },
          "until_done": {
            "default": true,
            "title": "Until Done",
            "type": "boolean"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::progress",
      "description": "One plain status line per task you (root) gave, then what needs your decision, then the scheduler. Read-only.\n\n        Per task: working / waiting on <agent> / stalled / blocked: <reason> / done / failed, who is busy, runs used\n        of the budget given (all runs of the task's team since it was given, against its budget plus every later grant),\n        time since the last activity, and for finished tasks the artifact paths and the runs returned. \"Needs you\"\n        lists every unread note, escalation, budget request, blocked/failed result and runtime notice, with its id.\n        task_id: only that task, in any state (default: open tasks and those finished in the last day).\n        wait_seconds (0-900, default 0): first wait until a task finishes, fails, blocks or stalls, or something new\n        needs the user, or the time is up, then answer; the answer starts with what changed. A task counts as in\n        progress, so the wait really waits, while its state is working/waiting, and also while it is blocked or\n        stalled but an agent below it is running or can run (unread mail that wakes it, budget left): for example the\n        lead of a blocked task right after you granted it runs and called start. It answers at once only when nothing\n        in the org can run, and ends early when the last thing that could run stops. Use it when the user wants to be\n        told when the work is done: tell them you will wait now, call progress(wait_seconds=...) and repeat as long\n        as they want (a turn cannot notify them later). Never poll with shell sleeps. Without wait_seconds it answers\n        \"status?\".\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "task_id": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Task Id"
          },
          "wait_seconds": {
            "default": 0,
            "title": "Wait Seconds",
            "type": "integer"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "not_found": [],
  "note": "These tools are now loaded for the rest of this session. To RUN one, call tool_call with { \"tool_id\": \"namespace::tool\", \"arguments\": { ... } } (use the tool_id shown for each result, and arguments matching its input_schema). Do not call tool_load again for tools you have already loaded."
}

{
  "loaded": [
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::observe",
      "description": "Read-only look at how the organization is running. view=\n        \"now\": what runs, what is queued and why, what waits on you, errors of the last 15 min.\n        \"trace\" (target=root task id): every message, run, tool call and refusal of one request, with time spent\n        queued, running and waiting on you. \"metrics\" (since=15m|24h|7d|ISO, by=agent|tool|service|trace): runs,\n        failures, refusal rates, latency percentiles, budget spent. \"events\" (target=agent, trace id or kind,\n        errors_only): the raw record. \"check\": is the runtime consistent (budget, messages, stuck runs)?",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "view": {
            "default": "now",
            "title": "View",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "target": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Target"
          },
          "since": {
            "default": "24h",
            "title": "Since",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "by": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "By"
          },
          "errors_only": {
            "default": false,
            "title": "Errors Only",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "limit": {
            "default": 50,
            "title": "Limit",
            "type": "integer"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::inbox",
      "description": "The messages for this run. For root (the human) this lists unread messages and marks them read.",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::health",
      "description": "Health report (stuck, expensive, low-quality, wasteful, idle, paused) for an agent and its subtree.\n\n        agent: yourself or an agent in your own subtree (root may ask about anyone). Default: your own subtree\n        (root: the whole organization). Use it to decide whom to follow up with, rework, re-budget or retire.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "agent": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Agent"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "not_found": [],
  "note": "These tools are now loaded for the rest of this session. To RUN one, call tool_call with { \"tool_id\": \"namespace::tool\", \"arguments\": { ... } } (use the tool_id shown for each result, and arguments matching its input_schema). Do not call tool_load again for tools you have already loaded."
}

{
  "loaded": [
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::send",
      "description": "Send a note: a question, information, or an escalation.\n\n        Allowed recipients: your parent, your direct reports, your siblings, or the sender of the message\n        you reply to (set reply_to to its id). budget: runs to move along with the note (optional): extra runs\n        granted to a direct report, or unneeded runs given back to your PARENT (never to a sibling). Runs you\n        have left return to your parent by themselves with your final `done`/`failed` report when nothing else\n        is open for you; use this only to give some back earlier. To pull unspent runs BACK from an idle direct\n        report instead (budget stranded in a team that cannot use it), use `reclaim`.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "to": {
            "title": "To",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "body": {
            "title": "Body",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": {
            "default": "",
